# Line endings are load-bearing here, which is not obvious.
#
# The self-updater verifies every downloaded file against a size and a SHA-256
# recorded in update/manifest.json, and that manifest is generated from the
# working tree by tools/make_release.py. If git normalises CRLF to LF on
# commit, raw.githubusercontent.com serves bytes that do not match what was
# hashed -- so every device that tried to update would download the release,
# fail verification, and refuse it. The failure is total and silent as to its
# cause: "expected 12071 bytes, got 11983".
#
# So: one line ending everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree on
# every platform, including a Windows checkout. Then what make_release hashes
# is what git stores is what the updater downloads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything genuinely binary must be exempt, or the rule above corrupts it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.epub binary
*.zip binary
